    "created_at": "2023-10-05T08:54:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-05T08:54:27Z",
    "body": "I made progress on CSP https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-csp/pull/621.\r\n\r\nOne thing: I realized that the various \"is request blocked\" algorithms actually have side effects (reporting violations), hence, opposite to what I was proposing before, I have the impression that a more verbose formulation (calling \"if **determining whether response is blocked by Content Security Policy** given *response* returns true\") is more appropriate, since it emphasises that the algorithm does more than just returning a boolean.",
